PHASE 5 OBJECTIVE: Build all 4 AI features. AI calls go through Cloudflare Pages Functions (server-side proxy) — NEVER directly from frontend.

CLOUDFLARE PAGES FUNCTIONS SETUP:
Create folder: functions/api/ai/
Each function reads these environment variables (set in Cloudflare dashboard — not in .env):
- CF_ACCOUNT_ID
- CF_GATEWAY_NAME
- CF_AI_TOKEN (Cloudflare AI API token)

Base URL for all AI calls inside functions:
https://gateway.ai.cloudflare.com/v1/${CF_ACCOUNT_ID}/${CF_GATEWAY_NAME}/workers-ai/

All functions: POST method, JSON body, return JSON response, CORS headers for your domain.

1. FUNCTION: functions/api/ai/recipe.ts
- Accepts: { ingredients: string[], dietary: string, cookTime: string, difficulty: string }
- System prompt: "You are a professional healthy food chef. Generate a detailed healthy recipe..."
- Model: @cf/meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct
- Returns: { title, description, ingredients: [{amount, unit, name}], instructions: [{step, text}], nutrition: {calories, protein, carbs, fat, fiber}, prepTime, cookTime, servings, dietaryLabels }
- Response must be valid JSON only

2. FUNCTION: functions/api/ai/meal-plan.ts
- Accepts: { duration: 1|7|30, dietary: string, budget: 'low'|'medium'|'high', preferences: string[] }
- Returns: structured meal plan JSON: { days: [{ day, breakfast, lunch, dinner, snacks: [], totalCalories }] }
- Each meal: { name, description, estimatedCalories, prepTime }

3. FUNCTION: functions/api/ai/chat.ts
- Accepts: { messages: [{role: 'user'|'assistant', content: string}], userPreferences?: string }
- System prompt: "You are a friendly, knowledgeable healthy food and nutrition assistant..."
- Returns: { reply: string }
- Maintains conversation context via message history

4. FUNCTION: functions/api/ai/image-analyze.ts
- Accepts: multipart form with image file
- Converts image to base64, sends to LLaVA model
- Model: @cf/llava-hf/llava-1.5-7b-hf
- Prompt: "Analyze this food image. Identify the food items, estimate portions, provide approximate nutritional information..."
- Returns: { foods: [{name, portion, calories, protein, carbs, fat}], healthierAlternatives: string[], disclaimer: string }

RATE LIMITING IN FUNCTIONS:
- Read x-user-id header (sent from frontend: auth user id or 'guest')
- Guest: max 3 requests per hour per IP (use KV or simple in-memory counter)
- If limit exceeded: return 429 with { error: 'rate_limit', message: '...' }

